   "created_at": "2026-07-18T01:18:29+00:00",
   "body_html": "<!--[if BLOCK]><![endif]-->            <p>Hello again! I managed to use the power of AI to invert the scroll effect. If anyone else is interested in learning how to do that I could happily DM you the instructions. Though for CWX (I\u2019m sure you likely already know) but I simply added a NEG line between the two \u201ccallvirt\u201d lines that \u201cget value\u201d and \u201cset scroll sensitivity\u201d. attached is a link to a screenshot of where I did this. It is line 85 that I added.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://i.gyazo.com/5255dd2e1315e8fae967543eddfd8b2b.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">https://i.gyazo.com/5255dd2e1315e8fae967543eddfd8b2b.png</a></p>\n\n        <!--[if ENDBLOCK]><![endif]-->",
